<p>
I edit a lot of transcripts,
and I've also been dictating to my computer more and more
for both prose and voice commands.
Speech recognition is pretty accurate, but there are some terms that it tends to get wrong.
There are also some terms that I find hard to say, like sometimes my brain will just hiccup and I'll end up saying "start screaming" instead of "start streaming".
I want to make it really easy to correct a misrecognized word throughout my current buffer
and save it for future edits.
</p>

<p>
One of the advantages of doing this kind of replacement within Emacs instead of a separate dictation tool is that I can use it for both editing text (like transcripts of other people's presentations) as well as pre-process the speech recognition results when I dictate or use voice commands to control Emacs.
I can even use it to start gradually getting my transcripts to follow Emacs keybinding conventions, like C-c instead of "control c", and for finicky capitalization like LaTeX.
</p>

