<div id="outline-container-orge603845" class="outline-3">
<h3 id="orge603845"><span class="section-number-3">3.</span> <a href="https://sachachua.com/blog/feed/index.xml#orge603845">Making changes with substitute.el</a></h3>
<div class="outline-text-3" id="text-3">
<p>
I like using <a href="https://protesilaos.com/emacs/substitute">Prot's substitute.el</a>.
I bind <code>substitute-target-in-buffer</code> to <code>C-;</code> . I can either replace the current word or select
a couple of words if I think I need to be more specific.
I ignore "SPEAKER_&hellip;" because then I can use the same shortcut to easily change speaker identification in transcripts.
</p>


<div class="org-src-container">
<pre class="src src-emacs-lisp"><code>(<span class="org-keyword">defvar</span> <span class="org-variable-name">sacha-substitute-save-changes</span> <span class="org-string">"SPEAKER_"</span>
  <span class="org-doc">"Non-nil means save changes to `</span><span class="org-doc"><span class="org-constant">sacha-subed-common-edits</span></span><span class="org-doc">'.</span>
<span class="org-doc">If this is a string, it is treated as a regular expression, and only</span>
<span class="org-doc">strings that do NOT match this regular expression will get saved.</span>
<span class="org-doc">If this is a function, call it with the target string. It should return</span>
<span class="org-doc">non-nil if the substitution should be saved."</span>)

(<span class="org-keyword">defun</span> <span class="org-function-name">sacha-substitute-save-common-edits</span> (target sub count scope)
  <span class="org-doc">"Keep track of changes so I can add them to `</span><span class="org-doc"><span class="org-constant">sacha-subed-common-edits</span></span><span class="org-doc">'."</span>
  (<span class="org-keyword">when</span> (<span class="org-keyword">cond</span>
         ((functionp sacha-substitute-save-changes)
          (funcall sacha-substitute-save-changes target))
         ((stringp sacha-substitute-save-changes)
          (not (string-match sacha-substitute-save-changes target)))
         (t
          sacha-substitute-save-changes))
    (customize-save-variable
     <span class="org-highlight-quoted-quote">'</span><span class="org-highlight-quoted-symbol">sacha-subed-common-edits</span>
     (cons (list sub target)
           sacha-subed-common-edits))))
</code></pre>
</div>


<div class="org-src-container">
<pre class="src src-emacs-lisp"><code>(<span class="org-keyword">use-package</span> substitute
<span class="org-builtin">:bind</span> (<span class="org-string">"C-;"</span> . substitute-target-in-buffer)
      <span class="org-builtin">:config</span>
      (<span class="org-keyword">setq</span> substitute-fixed-letter-case t)
      (add-hook <span class="org-highlight-quoted-quote">'</span><span class="org-highlight-quoted-symbol">substitute-post-replace-functions</span> <span class="org-highlight-quoted-quote">#'</span><span class="org-highlight-quoted-symbol">substitute-report-operation</span>)
      (add-hook <span class="org-highlight-quoted-quote">'</span><span class="org-highlight-quoted-symbol">substitute-post-replace-functions</span> <span class="org-highlight-quoted-quote">#'</span><span class="org-highlight-quoted-symbol">sacha-substitute-save-common-edits</span>))
</code></pre>
</div>


<p>
<code>customize-save-variable</code> is in charge of saving the changes after I replace something with susbtitute.el.
If I want to remove or edit entries, I can use <code>M-x customize-variable</code> to change <code>sacha-subed-common-edits</code>.
</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="outline-container-orge07758c" class="outline-3">
<h3 id="orge07758c"><span class="section-number-3">4.</span> <a href="https://sachachua.com/blog/feed/index.xml#orge07758c">Correcting the errors</a></h3>
<div class="outline-text-3" id="text-4">
<p>
Then I have some functions that make the changes automatically or interactively.
</p>


<div class="org-src-container">
<pre class="src src-emacs-lisp"><code><span class="org-comment-delimiter">;;;</span><span class="org-comment">###</span><span class="org-comment"><span class="org-warning">autoload</span></span>
(<span class="org-keyword">defun</span> <span class="org-function-name">sacha-subed-fix-common-errors</span> ()
  (<span class="org-keyword">interactive</span> )
  (<span class="org-keyword">let</span> (done entry correction)
    (<span class="org-keyword">while</span> (<span class="org-keyword">and</span>
            (not done)
            (<span class="org-keyword">setq</span> entry (sacha-subed-find-next-fix-point)))
      (<span class="org-keyword">setq</span> correction (<span class="org-keyword">if</span> (listp entry) (car entry) entry))
      (<span class="org-keyword">if</span> (<span class="org-keyword">let</span> ((case-fold-search nil))
            (looking-at (regexp-quote correction)))
          (forward-word 1)
        (<span class="org-keyword">if</span> (called-interactively-p <span class="org-highlight-quoted-quote">'</span><span class="org-highlight-quoted-symbol">any</span>)
            (<span class="org-keyword">let*</span> ((c (read-char (format <span class="org-string">"%s (yn.): "</span> correction))))
              (<span class="org-keyword">cond</span>
               ((= c ?y) (replace-match correction t t))
               ((= c ?n) (goto-char (match-end 0)))
               ((= c ?j) (subed-mpv-jump-to-current-subtitle))
               ((= c ?.) (<span class="org-keyword">setq</span> done t))))
          (replace-match correction t t))))))

<span class="org-comment-delimiter">;;;</span><span class="org-comment">###</span><span class="org-comment"><span class="org-warning">autoload</span></span>
(<span class="org-keyword">defun</span> <span class="org-function-name">sacha-subed-fix-common-errors-from-start</span> ()
  <span class="org-doc">"Change common errors in this buffer."</span>
  (<span class="org-keyword">interactive</span>)
  (goto-char (point-min))
  (sacha-subed-fix-common-errors))

<span class="org-comment-delimiter">;;;</span><span class="org-comment">###</span><span class="org-comment"><span class="org-warning">autoload</span></span>
(<span class="org-keyword">defun</span> <span class="org-function-name">sacha-subed-fix-common-errors-in-text</span> (text)
  <span class="org-doc">"Change common errors in TEXT."</span>
  (<span class="org-keyword">interactive</span>)
  (<span class="org-keyword">with-temp-buffer</span>
    (insert text)
    (goto-char (point-min))
    (sacha-subed-fix-common-errors)
    (buffer-string)))

<span class="org-comment-delimiter">;;;</span><span class="org-comment">###</span><span class="org-comment"><span class="org-warning">autoload</span></span>
(<span class="org-keyword">defun</span> <span class="org-function-name">sacha-subed-find-next-fix-point</span> ()
  (<span class="org-keyword">when</span> (re-search-forward
         (format <span class="org-string">"\\_&lt;</span><span class="org-string"><span class="org-regexp-grouping-backslash">\\</span></span><span class="org-string"><span class="org-regexp-grouping-construct">(</span></span><span class="org-string">%s</span><span class="org-string"><span class="org-regexp-grouping-backslash">\\</span></span><span class="org-string"><span class="org-regexp-grouping-construct">)</span></span><span class="org-string">\\_&gt;"</span>
                 (downcase
                  (string-join
                   (seq-mapcat
                    (<span class="org-keyword">lambda</span> (o)
                      (<span class="org-keyword">if</span> (listp o)
                          (<span class="org-keyword">if</span> (string= (car o) <span class="org-string">""</span>) (cdr o) o)
                        (list o)))
                    sacha-subed-common-edits)
                   <span class="org-string">"</span><span class="org-string"><span class="org-regexp-grouping-backslash">\\</span></span><span class="org-string"><span class="org-regexp-grouping-construct">|</span></span><span class="org-string">"</span>)))
         nil t)
    (goto-char (match-beginning 0))
    (seq-find
     (<span class="org-keyword">lambda</span> (o)
       (<span class="org-keyword">if</span> (listp o)
           (seq-find (<span class="org-keyword">lambda</span> (s)
                       (<span class="org-keyword">save-match-data</span>
                         (string-match
                          (format <span class="org-string">"\\_&lt;%s\\&gt;"</span> (downcase s))
                          (downcase (match-string 0))))) <span class="org-warning">o)</span>
         (string= (downcase o) (downcase (match-string 0)))))
     sacha-subed-common-edits)))

<span class="org-comment-delimiter">;;;</span><span class="org-comment">###</span><span class="org-comment"><span class="org-warning">autoload</span></span>
(<span class="org-keyword">defun</span> <span class="org-function-name">sacha-subed-fix-common-error</span> ()
  (<span class="org-keyword">interactive</span>)
  (<span class="org-keyword">let</span> ((entry (sacha-subed-find-next-fix-point)))
    (replace-match (<span class="org-keyword">if</span> (listp entry) (car entry) entry) t t)))
</code></pre>
</div>


<p>
Then I can call <code>sacha-subedf-fix-common-errors-in-text</code> from my <a href="https://sachachua.com/dotemacs#multimedia-whisper">whisper-insert-text-at-point</a> functions, and
<code>sacha-subed-fix-common-errors-from-start</code> from <a href="https://sachachua.com/dotemacs#streaming-download-and-post-process">sacha-stream-prepare-transcript-for-editing</a>.
</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="outline-container-org0de6da8" class="outline-3">
<h3 id="org0de6da8"><span class="section-number-3">5.</span> <a href="https://sachachua.com/blog/feed/index.xml#org0de6da8">Other ways to define the correction</a></h3>
<div class="outline-text-3" id="text-5">
<p>
Here's another function to define a correction if you don't want to use substitute.el.
</p>


<div class="org-src-container">
<pre class="src src-emacs-lisp"><code><span class="org-comment-delimiter">;;;</span><span class="org-comment">###</span><span class="org-comment"><span class="org-warning">autoload</span></span>
(<span class="org-keyword">defun</span> <span class="org-function-name">sacha-subed-add-common-edit</span> (beg end replacement)
  <span class="org-doc">"Add this word to the misrecognized words."</span>
  (<span class="org-keyword">interactive</span>
   (<span class="org-keyword">let</span> ((beg (<span class="org-keyword">if</span> (region-active-p) (min (point) (mark))
                (skip-syntax-backward <span class="org-string">"w"</span>)
                (point)))
         (end (<span class="org-keyword">if</span> (region-active-p) (max (point) (mark))
                (<span class="org-keyword">save-excursion</span> (forward-word 1) (point)))))
     (list beg end
           (completing-read
            (format <span class="org-string">"Replacement (%s): "</span> (buffer-substring beg end))
            (mapcar (<span class="org-keyword">lambda</span> (o) (<span class="org-keyword">if</span> (stringp o) o (car o))) sacha-subed-common-edits)))))
  (customize-set-variable
   <span class="org-highlight-quoted-quote">'</span><span class="org-highlight-quoted-symbol">sacha-subed-common-edits</span>
   (<span class="org-keyword">cond</span>
    ((member replacement sacha-subed-common-edits)
     (cons (list replacement (buffer-substring-no-properties beg end))
           (delete replacement sacha-subed-common-edits)))
    ((assoc replacement sacha-subed-common-edits)
     (setcdr (assoc replacement sacha-subed-common-edits)
             (append (list replacement) (cdr (assoc replacement sacha-subed-common-edits))))
     sacha-subed-common-edits)
    (t
     (<span class="org-keyword">push</span> (list replacement (buffer-substring-no-properties beg end))
           sacha-subed-common-edits))))
  (delete-region beg end)
  (insert replacement))
</code></pre>
</div>


<p>
At some point, I really should abstract this out to its own package, because it's just so useful.
Other people have actually managed to get it to work, which is always a nice milestone.
Anyway, here it is, in case it's helpful for you too!
</p>
